# Duration components beyond machine integers

A duration holds its components as machine integers: a component that does
not fit one is the runtime error of integers too large for a computation,
reported with the path of the JSON value.

```catala
declaration scope I:
  input d content duration
  output same content duration

scope I:
  definition same equals d
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope I --input {"d":{"days":"99999999999999999999"}}
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: an integer is too large for this computation.
│  Reading the JSON value at /d/days.
│
└─
#return code 123#
```

A component that is not an integer is refused by the schema:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope I --input {"d":{"days":1.5}}
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Failed to validate JSON:
│    At /d/days, unexpected number 1.5 instead of an integer (integral number or string of digits)
│  
│  Expected JSON object of the form:
│    { "d": $duration }
│    $duration:
│      /* Catala duration */
│      { "years"?: $integer,
│        "months"?: $integer,
│        "days"?: $integer }
│    $integer:
│      /* Catala Integer */
│      integer | /^-?[0-9]+$/
│
└─
#return code 123#
```
